course: dictionary
lesson: 3216
title: Enough: as much as you need
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Enough means as much as you need or want. «You have enough money to buy the book.» The word tells you the amount is right: not too little, and nothing is missing.
explain: Enough can come after another word to show that a need is met: «Is the water hot enough?» Here enough follows hot, so it means hot to the needed amount. To check, ask yourself: is there enough for what is needed?
explain: Enough can also stand alone as a pronoun: «Have we got enough?» Be careful with «That's enough!», which means stop now. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Enough means as much as you need or want.
fact: Enough after a word, such as big enough or fast enough, means the amount is right for what is needed.
fact: «More than enough» means extra, and «not enough» means too little.
fact: «Enough is enough» is a phrase that means stop now, because the limit has been reached.
fact: In maths, you can check whether you have enough by comparing what you have with what you need.
exercise: «Saving means putting money aside, week after week, until you have enough for something bigger than one week's money can buy.» What does enough mean in this sentence? | Too much to carry | *As much as you need | Nothing at all | A small coin
exercise: Ruby has 8 pounds and needs 12 pounds for a game. How many more pounds does she need to have enough? | 20 | *4 | 8 | 2
exercise: «Is the water hot enough to make tea?» Enough comes after which word? | Make | Water | *Hot | Tea
test: «An open oven door and the inside of the oven are hot enough to burn skin instantly.» What does hot enough mean here? | Cold enough to freeze | *Hot to the needed amount to burn skin | Warm enough for bread | Slightly warm
test: «Plants need enough light and water to grow.» What does enough mean here? | Too much light and water | Less than the plant can see | *Just the right amount for growing | Something that stops growth
exam: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt lead.» What does enough mean in hot enough to melt lead? | *Hot to the needed amount to melt lead | Cool enough to swim in | Enough of a hot drink | Too hot to bear
